The policy re-reads the camera, takes the median with the reading you gave, and goes to that pose first, lowering in 0.5 mm steps near the surface so a misaligned peg touches the block face gently and retracts instead of colliding. The reported yaw of -34° is outside the cell's stated 0 ± 15° range, even allowing for the 90° symmetry, so I did not trust either source blindly. If the measured pose fails, the policy tries small yaw corrections, then sweeps the ±15° range, then small position offsets, all within the call budget; I have not run it against the simulator.
